      {
        "id": 264109,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2025-10-23T12:23:59.528Z",
        "cooked": "<p>“This letter continues”…or, “The slaughter continues”?</p>\n<p>It’s pretty obvious to me that the “golden orb” Doc gives Writhe…it’s a pill!</p>\n<p>This episode is semi-accidentally also the Oblivion Shards episode, since no other characters are walking around using shards - Proletariat and the Brothers Cosmic were transformed by exposure to shards, but none of them kept these and continued being transformed by them.  A thing I really love about OblivAeon is that he’s not just a grand cosmic destroyer, he’s a <em>creator</em> of things which destroy.  The shards are trying to turn all the Void Guardians into Scions, and they’re all resisting, some better than others.  It’s really cool.</p>\n<p>I fully endorse and share Adam’s point on Shower Strangers.  If I have to be naked in a room where another man is also naked, I would e substantially happier to be killed with a knife over any other possible interaction.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2025-10-23T12:56:53.962Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
